# Pipeline Dry Run — Results

Date: 2026-07-22
Strategy used: `DryRunEMACross` (EMA20/EMA50 crossover, BTC-USD, Kraken Pro Futures, 1h, market orders, fixed size). Deliberately un-tuned — performance numbers below are noise and irrelevant. This document validates **mechanics only**.

---

## 1. Data availability

Requested import of BTC-USD from 2023-01-01, but the database already held BTC/ETH/SOL data back to 2022-04-01 from an earlier import session (per ROADMAP.md). Verified via direct Postgres query (the `get_existing_candles` / `get_candles` MCP tools could not answer this — see §Findings).

| Symbol | First candle (1m, UTC) | Last candle (1m, UTC) | Usable history |
|---|---|---|---|
| BTC-USD | 2022-04-01 00:00 | 2026-07-22 09:24 | ~4.31 years |
| ETH-USD | 2022-04-01 00:00 | 2026-07-22 09:25 | ~4.31 years |
| SOL-USD | 2022-04-01 00:00 | 2026-07-22 09:25 | ~4.31 years |
| XRP-USD | 2023-01-01 00:00 (partial) | import still running at report time | **incomplete — see below** |

BTC-USD 1h aggregate: **37,762 candles** (2022-04-01 00:00 → 2026-07-22 09:00), computed by grouping the underlying 1-minute candles into hourly buckets — Jesse stores only `1m` candles and builds all other timeframes on the fly.

**XRP-USD import did not finish inside the dry run window.** It was launched in parallel with ETH and SOL, and while those two finished in under a minute, XRP crawled (0.5% → 15% over ~15 minutes, throttled). This reproduces the exact issue already logged in ROADMAP.md: **parallel imports get rate-limited; only sequential imports are reliable.** The import is still running in the background against import_id `16a8cc11-0ac0-4482-bb51-412ddf890db8`; XRP's true earliest-candle date is not yet confirmed (only 2023-01-01, the requested start, is confirmed so far).

### Gap scan (BTC-USD, full history)

- **Timestamp continuity: perfect.** Zero missing 1-minute timestamps across the full 2022-04-01 → 2026-07-22 range.
- **Zero-volume candles: 1,478,205 of 2,265,685 (65.2%)** of all 1-minute candles have `open=high=low=close` (flat) and `volume=0` — these are synthetic forward-filled placeholders, not real trades.
- At the **1-hour** granularity actually used for trading: **37,762 hours total, of which 22,325 (59.1%) have zero volume for the entire hour.** Longest streak: **51 consecutive zero-volume hours** (2025-01-09 08:00 → 2025-01-11 10:00 UTC). Similar ~50-hour streaks recur roughly every 2-3 weeks throughout the whole history, not just around known stress events (Luna/FTX).
- **This is not confined to history** — a sample of the most recent 3 days (2026-07-19 → 2026-07-22) showed 3,919 of 4,315 1-minute candles (90.8%) zero-volume, so it is an ongoing condition, not a stale/fixed artifact.
- **Cross-symbol check — this is the critical detail:** ETH-USD, SOL-USD, and XRP-USD (partial) all show the *same* ~59.1–59.3% zero-volume-hour rate as BTC-USD, despite having very different real-world liquidity profiles. Genuine market thinness would not produce near-identical percentages across BTC and XRP. This strongly suggests a **systematic artifact in the Kraken Pro Futures data driver/import path** in this Jesse install (wrong/thin instrument mapping, or an OHLC endpoint returning sparse data that gets forward-filled) rather than real illiquidity.
- **See Findings/Blocker below — this needs root-cause investigation before the real research run.**

---

## 2. Backtest mechanics

One-year backtest, BTC-USD, 1h, 2023-01-01 → 2024-01-01.

- **Execution time: 1.0 second.**
- Trades: 103 (51 long / 52 short) | Sharpe: 0.79 | Max drawdown: -32.87% | Net profit: 29.9%
- **Fees confirmed active and material:** total fees $1,281.07 vs. net profit $2,990.32 (gross profit $19,958.62, gross loss -$16,968.30). Fee rate in Jesse's config for Kraken Pro Futures is a single flat **0.05%** (`fee: 0.0005`), which is exactly the Kraken **taker** rate — correct, since this strategy only uses market orders (100% taker fills).
- **Caveat for the real run:** Jesse's exchange config exposes only **one flat fee rate per exchange** — there is no separate maker/taker split. That's fine here (all-market-order strategy), but the main research prompt prefers **limit-order entries** and wants the 0.02%/0.05% maker/taker difference modeled correctly. As configured, Jesse cannot natively distinguish a limit (maker) fill from a market (taker) fill fee-wise — this will need a workaround (e.g. a conservative single taker-rate assumption for limit-heavy strategies, or manual fee handling in strategy code) before the real run scores anything that relies on maker fees.
- **Slippage: no configurable slippage parameter exists anywhere in Jesse's config** (checked `get_config` and `get_backtest_config` — no `slippage` field at any level). Inspecting actual trade fills: orders execute at the **open of the candle immediately following the signal candle** (standard bar-based fill), with no additional stochastic/pessimistic slippage layered on top. If "pessimistic slippage" (per the main prompt) is required, it is **not available as a config toggle** and must be modeled manually inside strategy code (e.g. padding entry/exit price by a few bps).

---

## 3. Walk-forward mechanics

Real first-candle date (2022-04-01) matches the main prompt's assumption exactly, so fold boundaries need **no date adjustment** — folds 1-3 from the main prompt were used as-is:

| Fold | IS window | OOS window |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 2022-04-01 → 2023-10-31 | 2023-11-01 → 2024-04-30 |
| 2 | 2022-10-01 → 2024-04-30 | 2024-05-01 → 2024-10-31 |
| 3 | 2023-04-01 → 2024-10-31 | 2024-11-01 → 2025-04-30 |

**One mechanical failure, fixed and documented:** Fold 1's IS backtest, run with `start_date=2022-04-01` (the literal first available candle), **failed** with:
> `Missing candles for BTC-USD on Kraken Pro Futures. This run needs data from 2022-03-14 to 2023-10-31 (which includes 210 warm-up candles before the start date).`

Jesse always needs a warm-up buffer (210 candles per `warm_up_candles` config) *before* the requested start date. Since 2022-04-01 is genuinely the first candle in the database, there's nothing to warm up from. **Fix applied:** pushed Fold 1's IS start to 2022-04-25 (retried successfully). **Action item for the real run: any fold whose IS window starts at the raw first-candle date will fail the same way — start it ~2-3 weeks later, or treat the effective usable history as starting ~2022-04-19 to 2022-04-25, not 2022-04-01.**

All 6 backtests (after the fix) completed without further errors, in 0.36-1.08 seconds each:

| Session | Trades | Sharpe | Max DD |
|---|---|---|---|
| Fold1-IS (adj. start 2022-04-25) | 164 | 0.17 | -46.24% |
| Fold1-OOS | 52 | 2.54 | -14.56% |
| Fold2-IS | 164 | 1.24 | -32.85% |
| Fold2-OOS | 42 | 1.18 | -23.15% |
| Fold3-IS | 155 | 1.23 | -23.96% |
| Fold3-OOS | 45 | 1.55 | -18.96% |

Numbers are noise (untuned strategy) and expected to be bad/inconsistent — the only thing being validated is that all 6 runs complete inside available history without errors, which they now do.

